  "goodToKnow": "Das Vernichtungslager is an extermination camp, built by Nazi Germany in occupied Poland primarily for the systematic murder of Jews in the Holocaust: Auschwitz-Birkenau, Treblinka, Sobibor, Belzec, Chelmno, Majdanek. Konzentrationslager (KZ) were camps of imprisonment and forced labour, where many also died. Memorials (Gedenkstätten) keep the memory alive. The plural is the same."
